# SUMMARY OF THE TWO CURVES (the H-B6 result):
#   bind: ~0.735 (earlier 0.1 diagnostic weight) -> 0.57 (step 500 @ 0.42)
#         -> 0.31 (1000) -> 0.22 (2000) -> ~0.205 plateau (2500) -> ~0.20 (3000)
#         plateau cos recovery ~0.80, past the N=16 crosstalk floor (cos~0.25)
#   bpc : ~2.3 (500) -> 1.95 (1000) -> 1.74 (2000) -> 1.69 (2500) -> ~1.5 (3000)
#   => both fall in lockstep; no bpc stall/bump through the warmup->full-LR
#      transition (step 2000) or sustained full LR -> binding not stealing LM
#      capacity (co-descent also rules out a degenerate low-rank h collapse).
